d "d679ee8f-58d7-55d5-9199-5ee365b83298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "443df7a5-b8c5-5f97-a311-9bd695ebd981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244910} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dfe16e0-1455-5fce-9d3d-1d07558b58c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "41dfac52-4d1d-591c-8036-6625f46b98d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110494" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302051 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 1