ation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46f3e548-ea7a-5436-bed5-5b7a9a6026d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300320} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad8d28c-e868-5868-8413-6322f84a2fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300347} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0c5047-959e-5134-8822-7384bc80845a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300586} {:answer/id #uuid "cc271c4a-91a0-5cce-b573-018619a7dc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300982} {:answer/id #uuid "f7517fe5-d015-57e3-a049-a5efb53cec23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e0c5047-959e-5134-8822-7384bc80845a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300586} :answer-field/id #uuid "918cd991-3826-55e2-a035-fd8fa5f520dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90efc42e-c582-5ebf-b710-fc84d57b2391" :question/math-academy-id "q-32144" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134189 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21948faf-e95a-5edb-90cb-1da55120bdf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-3{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477799} {:answer/id #uuid "40e9e6a6-42dc-5c43-8d3d-b1154d529448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477856} {:answer/id #uuid "47c8ae66-6c47-5457-9c0b-2626458218ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477875} {:answer/id #uuid "51569822-4746-5054-a95a-35b8d1b9b4f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477901} {:answer/id #uuid "7ffad30d-316a-5348-befb-64ed01e69f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47c8ae66-6c47-5457-9c0b-2626458218ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477875} :answer-field/id #uuid "49db34c5-1a78-58e6-9b61-a2209475d815" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0972695d-55f6-56a5-a84e-e125e7bacf50" :question/math-academy-id "q-32145" :question/problem "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the second row of ${I}_{3}$ by $-\\frac{2}{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{2}:=-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f052266-a78d-53f6-a624-dbcfb60c6b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300017} {:answer/id #uuid "28489d41-fcfe-5fbd-aa9f-58d8c03fdfa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300156} {:answer/id #uuid "447d16d4-e4ed-5411-a267-a5cd72c6a62a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300301} {:answer/id #uuid "78150501-86d3-5ad2-b18d-3aa575407c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300553} {:answer/id #uuid "e840a680-6695-5b5e-b17d-1a0d7769e11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "447d16d4-e4ed-5411-a267-a5cd72c6a62a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300301} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8eef8d5-a521-5905-9cae-619b2505ad27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67780f7b-b335-51d6-8512-e61d1ae7ee4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32147" :question/problem "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by swapping the first and the second rows of ${I}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133744 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a9c3794-3d61-5c59-8f4c-0fba7faa0d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300081} {:answer/id #uuid "6036e44a-abe5-5908-af38-25d639e02c1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300456} {:answer/id #uuid "85975f0b-1702-5c99-8d51-dd63c624b6d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300631} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b73eaf-15e2-5527-a7eb-70edc5e8e657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300883} {:answer/id #uuid "dbeceeef-284b-50ec-b0a1-fe8def1b75fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85975f0b-1702-5c99-8d51-dd63c624b6d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300631} :answer-field/id #uuid "66d99da3-9056-5439-b363-5f8b29fdcf4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d615245-8860-57bd-9182-e8271d3465f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-32148" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:ans