n/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329665 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "255b1ea2-ed27-596e-8626-b1b2d8321ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327258} {:answer/id #uuid "3fe72058-46a6-5a78-b84f-026a0b8b6b89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327493} {:answer/id #uuid "6ddbe7a4-e77d-5a9e-9478-88103a828d5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327886} {:answer/id #uuid "92b8adc9-9e6a-531d-b1f2-36d519bd89c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328212} {:answer/id #uuid "ed8ca3eb-b5a5-566a-84f2-4571a314fee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed8ca3eb-b5a5-566a-84f2-4571a314fee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329015} :answer-field/id #uuid "a230bae0-2871-57b7-b729-3347db98f89d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af9357b2-c67e-5916-b938-27da4594eabf" :question/math-academy-id "q-42534" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53e4aa25-aa86-58b1-88cf-facb2032bdf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477910} {:answer/id #uuid "68fb0bfb-fa69-50bd-bcf8-a76dee8e1e5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477947} {:answer/id #uuid "cc5d0d99-fe51-53e6-a1f9-3c79531f2797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=4{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478140} {:answer/id #uuid "d3040f50-dd20-53b9-8a20-03fe6e0d7152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478152} {:answer/id #uuid "d416fe18-761a-5049-aa24-46b59c66c8b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68fb0bfb-fa69-50bd-bcf8-a76dee8e1e5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477947} :answer-field/id #uuid "c60cb50c-be28-51c2-98b8-1d31746b4a4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f630631-31e9-5df2-8934-f227dd41371f" :question/math-academy-id "q-75107" :question/problem "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the third row of ${I}_{3}$ by $\\frac{5}{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{3}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3374bbd1-d32d-57b4-bc0a-11d4f8c904cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477833} {:answer/id #uuid "6cd3ff81-7364-581c-b9ed-863e2867bc0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477960} {:answer/id #uuid "842246db-ab67-57e3-8dc6-b1c77e9e5f24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478007} {:answer/id #uuid "ceed8c41-48e5-544e-ba38-45d59e032946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478146} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa9d752-e116-5522-887a-f0bcd1930d2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceed8c41-48e5-544e-ba38-45d59e032946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478146} :answer-field/id #uuid "c475651d-4b22-564c-b87f-67c6954787b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e13146e0-974e-5b74-8d7d-df8fb20c3089" :question/math-academy-id "q-75110" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation \n${R}_{1}:=\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{1}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{1}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}]}
